  "label": "The text 'I'm not that fucking retarded..' is mapped onto the visual entity 'woman_on_left'.",
  "description": "The text 'I'm not that fucking retarded..' is an explicit denial or insult directed at the speaker, who is visually represented by 'woman_on_left'. The meme uses the visual of the woman laughing to imply that she is the one being mocked — the 'I' in the text. The analogical mapping is that the woman_on_left is the person being referenced in the text, even though the text is framed as a self-deprecating or defensive statement. The visual of her laughing while holding a mug is mapped onto the textual persona of the speaker, who is denying being 'retarded' — a slur that targets intellectual disability. The mapping is between the textual speaker and the visual woman, who is the subject of the insult.",
